                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/315: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-20T11:00:00-03:00">December 20, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>344. Department’s 212 December 19, 1 p.m. Braden having repeated to me
                    Department’s 178, December 18, noon, I took occasion to discuss the matter with
                    Macedo Soares yesterday afternoon and he immediately instructed Rodriguez Alves
                    by telegraph in the sense desired. I so informed Braden yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
